CPU entropy_mul bisect — W22-1 chunk-2 follow-on
=================================================

Date: 2026-05-18
Host: $(uname -n)
Repo: jxl-encoder (sibling workspace --cpu-entropy-mul-bisect)
Parent commit: 6abfb9c9 (W22-1: content-aware entropy_mul gate, opt-in, default OFF)
Build features: __expert butteraugli-loop
Effort: 7

Harness: jxl-encoder/examples/cpu_entropy_mul_bisect.rs

Sweep design
------------
Stage A (screen): paired baseline (libjxl reference EntropyMulTable) vs
lifted (`LossyInternalParams::entropy_mul_table` override) across:
  IDENTITY ∈ {1.20, 1.30, 1.40, 1.50, 1.60}     (libjxl base = 1.0428)
  DCT2X2   ∈ {0.95, 0.9975, 1.045}              (libjxl base = 0.95)
  AFV      = 0.95   (PINNED at W22-1 lift)
  DCT4X8   = 0.98   (PINNED at W22-1 lift)
  d ∈ {0.5, 1.0, 2.0}
  5 gb82-sc screenshots: codec_wiki, imac_dark, imac_g3, terminal, windows95
  Total: 5 imgs × 5 ident × 3 dct2 × 3 dist + 15 baselines = 240 measurements

Stage B (photo validation): 5 CID22-512 photos × tuple = 30 measurements
  Tuple: IDENTITY=1.85, DCT2X2=1.15 (W22-1 default)
  (CPU_ENT_PHOTO_IDENT / CPU_ENT_PHOTO_DCT2 env vars to override.)

Methodology
-----------
Per cell: encode with reference table (baseline) and lifted table; decode
both with jxl-oxide in linear sRGB; measure Rust `butteraugli_linear`. The
PNG-metadata trap in `butteraugli_main` is avoided per CLAUDE.md.

TSV columns
-----------
stage           A | B
image           label
class           screen | photo
distance        target distance
identity        IDENTITY entropy_mul (lifted)
dct2x2          DCT2X2 entropy_mul (lifted)
afv             AFV entropy_mul (pinned at 0.95 W22-1)
dct4x8          DCT4X8 entropy_mul (pinned at 0.98 W22-1)
baseline_bytes  reference table encode bytes
lifted_bytes    lifted table encode bytes
baseline_bfly   reference table butteraugli
lifted_bfly     lifted table butteraugli
bytes_delta_pct (lifted - baseline) / baseline * 100
bfly_delta_pct  (lifted - baseline) / baseline * 100
baseline_ms     reference table encode wall ms
lifted_ms       lifted table encode wall ms

Headline
--------
NO winning tuple meets the chunk-2 acceptance gate
(median Δbytes ≤ 0.5 %, max(|Δbfly|) ≤ 2 %).

Lowest median Δbytes: IDENTITY=1.20, DCT2X2=1.045 → median Δbytes +0.136 %
  but max |Δbfly| = 18.45 % (terminal d=2 unstable, +18.45 % bfly).

Best stability: IDENTITY=1.40, DCT2X2=0.9975 → max |Δbfly| 14.97 %
  but median Δbytes +0.771 % (above 0.5 % gate).

Stage B photo at the W22-1 tuple shows -1.13 % median bytes / +20 % max
bfly — confirms photos are NOT bit-identical at the lifted table (the
override bypasses the content-aware gate).

Reproducer
----------
cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder --features '__expert butteraugli-loop' \
    --example cpu_entropy_mul_bisect -- \
    benchmarks/cpu_entropy_mul_bisect_2026-05-18.tsv
